<!-- =====================================================
     11 LUCKY
===================================================== -->

<section class="section" id="lucky">

    <div class="section-heading">

        <span class="section-kicker">
            11 • LUCKY
        </span>

        <h2>
            Lucky Mr. Rime
        </h2>

        <p>
            Lucky Mr. Rime is a special trade outcome. Lucky
            Pokémon are guaranteed to have a minimum IV floor
            and generally require less Stardust to power up.
        </p>

    </div>


    <div class="variant-card lucky-card">

        <div class="variant-icon">
            🍀
        </div>

        <strong>
            Lucky Mr. Rime
        </strong>

        <p>
            A desirable trading variant for collectors and
            players looking to reduce Stardust costs.
        </p>

    </div>


    <h3>
        Why Lucky Mr. Rime Can Be Useful
    </h3>


    <ul class="checklist">

        <li>
            Lucky trades provide a guaranteed IV floor.
        </li>

        <li>
            Lucky Pokémon receive reduced Stardust costs
            for power-ups.
        </li>

        <li>
            Lucky Mr. Rime can be useful for collectors.
        </li>

        <li>
            A lucky trade can produce a high-IV Mr. Rime.
        </li>

        <li>
            Lucky status does not automatically mean 100% IV.
        </li>

    </ul>


    <div class="feature-card">

        <strong>
            Lucky ≠ Hundo
        </strong>

        <p>
            A Lucky Mr. Rime can have excellent IVs, but Lucky
            status and perfect 15/15/15 IVs are separate
            characteristics.
        </p>

    </div>

</section>


