<!-- =====================================================
     23 FAQ
===================================================== -->

<section class="section" id="faq">

    <div class="section-heading">

        <span class="section-kicker">
            23 • FAQ
        </span>

        <h2>
            Mr. Rime FAQ
        </h2>

    </div>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What type is Mr. Rime?
        </summary>

        <p>
            Mr. Rime is an Ice/Psychic-type Pokémon.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is Mr. Rime weak against?
        </summary>

        <p>
            Mr. Rime is weak to Bug, Dark, Fire, Ghost, Rock
            and Steel-type attacks.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is Mr. Rime's Max CP?
        </summary>

        <p>
            Mr. Rime's Level 50 maximum CP is 3,196 with
            perfect IVs.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is Shiny Mr. Rime available?
        </summary>

        <p>
            Yes. Shiny Mr. Rime is available in Pokémon GO.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is Shadow Mr. Rime available?
        </summary>

        <p>
            Yes. Shadow Mr. Rime is available and retains its
            Ice/Psychic typing.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Can Shadow Mr. Rime be purified?
        </summary>

        <p>
            Eligible Shadow Mr. Rime can be purified. Players
            should compare the Shadow and purified versions
            before making the decision.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is a 100% Mr. Rime?
        </summary>

        <p>
            A 100% Mr. Rime has 15 Attack, 15 Defense and
            15 HP IVs.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Is Lucky Mr. Rime automatically a Hundo?
        </summary>

        <p>
            No. Lucky Pokémon have a minimum IV floor, but
            Lucky status does not guarantee 15/15/15 IVs.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is an XXL Mr. Rime?
        </summary>

        <p>
            XXL Mr. Rime is an oversized Mr. Rime belonging to
            the XXL size category.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is an XXS Mr. Rime?
        </summary>

        <p>
            XXS Mr. Rime is a very small Mr. Rime belonging to
            the XXS size category.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Does XXL Mr. Rime have higher Attack?
        </summary>

        <p>
            No. XXL status is a size classification and should
            not be treated as a direct Attack IV or battle-stat
            bonus.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            Does XXS Mr. Rime have lower Attack?
        </summary>

        <p>
            XXS status is primarily a size classification.
            Evaluate Attack using the Pokémon's actual IVs and
            battle stats.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            What is Mr. Rime's best Ice moveset?
        </summary>

        <p>
            Ice Shard and Triple Axel are the recommended
            Ice-focused moveset listed for Mr. Rime.
        </p>

    </details>


    <details>

        <summary>
            How does Galarian Mr. Mime evolve into Mr. Rime?
        </summary>

        <p>
            Galarian Mr. Mime evolves into Mr. Rime using
            50 Candy.
        </p>

    </details>

</section>


